at doesn't take itself too seriously.  If you want to blow up giant space bugs and aliens this is your game.  If you don't want to blow up giant space bugs this isn't the game for you and I want nothing to do with you.", "timestamp_created": 1599363286, "timestamp_updated": 1599363286, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.523809552192687988", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1562828575", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "75479632", "author": {"steamid": "76561198437525769", "personaname": "devjunkie", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198437525769/", "num_games_owned": 142, "num_reviews": 33, "playtime_forever": 6771, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 6771, "last_played": 1567578168, "avatar": "97837aad4d3d3fd9debfa9512b022c8045c2ea41"}, "language": "english", "review": "Chaotic nonstop upgrade madness\n\nSure the missions are repetitive, but you can get so many ridiculously new and powerful, or WTF is this, new weapons or vehicles!\n\nGood solo play, but really you need to play online with others to get much enjoyment out of it.  The story is ridiculous, but think of MXC mixed with every anime brought to the western world with a dabble of old skool voltron.\n\nlove, lol, and repeat", "timestamp_created": 1599305128, "timestamp_updated": 1599305128, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.476190477609634399", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1562828575", "reactions": []}]}